e="View this template">v</abbr></a></li><li class="nv-talk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Software_development_process" title="Template talk:Software development process"><abbr title="Discuss this template">t</abbr></a></li><li class="nv-edit"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:EditPage/Template:Software_development_process" title="Special:EditPage/Template:Software development process"><abbr title="Edit this template">e</abbr></a></li></ul></div></td></tr></tbody></table>

<p id="mwCA">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_development" title="Software development" id="mwCQ">software development</a>, <b id="mwCg">functional testing</b> is a form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_testing" title="Software testing" id="mwCw">software testing</a> that verifies whether a system meets its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functional_requirement" title="Functional requirement" id="mwDA">functional requirements</a>.<sup about="#mwt11" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ISO24765_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ISO24765&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ISO24765-1&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ISO24765-1" id="mwDQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDw">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt14" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-2&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwEQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEw">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFA">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwFQ">Generally, functional testing is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black-box_testing" title="Black-box testing" id="mwFg">black-box</a>, meaning the internal program structure is ignored (unlike for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White-box_testing" title="White-box testing" id="mwFw">white-box testing</a>).<sup about="#mwt17" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-KanerFalkNguyen1999_3-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;KanerFalkNguyen1999&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-KanerFalkNguyen1999-3&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-KanerFalkNguyen1999-3" id="mwGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGw">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwHA">Sometimes, functional testing is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quality_assurance" title="Quality assurance" id="mwHQ">quality assurance</a> (QA) process.<sup about="#mwt20" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Prasad_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Prasad&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Prasad-4&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Prasad-4" id="mwHg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIA">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwIg">As a form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System_testing" title="System testing" id="mwIw">system testing</a>, functional testing tests slices of functionality of the whole system. 
Despite similar naming, functional testing is not testing the code of a single <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Function_(computer_programming)" title="Function (computer programming)" id="mwJA">function</a>.</p>

<p id="mwJQ">The concept of incorporating testing earlier in the delivery cycle is not restricted to functional testing.<sup about="#mwt23" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-5&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwJg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKA">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwKg" data-mw="{&quot;autoGenerated&quot;:true}"></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwKw" aria-labelledby="Types"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Types">Types</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Functional_testing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Types"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwLA">Functional testing includes but is not limited to:<sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-KanerFalkNguyen1999_3-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;KanerFalkNguyen1999&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-KanerFalkNguyen1999-3" id="mwLQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwMQ" aria-labelledby="Sanity_testing"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Sanity_testing">Sanity testing</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Functional_testing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Sanity testing"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div class="excerpt-block" about="#mwt25" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwMg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Excerpt&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Excerpt&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Sanity testing&quot;},&quot;only&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;paragraphs&quot;},&quot;paragraphs&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1353838603" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt26" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Excerpt/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}">.mw-parser-output .excerpt-hat .mw-editsection-like{font-style:normal}</style><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt27" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable dablink excerpt-hat selfref">These paragraphs are an excerpt from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanity_check" title="Sanity check">Sanity check</a>.<span class="mw-editsection-like plainlinks"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Sanity_check&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Sanity_check&amp;action=edit">edit</a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><div class="excerpt">
<p>A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanity_check" title="Sanity check">sanity check</a> or sanity test is a basic test to quickly evaluate whether a claim or the result of a calculation can possibly be true. It is a simple check to see if the produced material is rational (that the material's creator was thinking rationally, applying <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanity" title="Sanity">sanity</a>). The point of a sanity test is to rule out certain classes of obviously false results, not to catch every possible error. A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rule-of-thumb" title="Rule-of-thumb" class="mw-redirect">rule-of-thumb</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Back-of-the-envelope_calculation" title="Back-of-the-envelope calculation">back-of-the-envelope calculation</a> may be checked to perform the test. The advantage of performing an initial sanity test is that of speedily evaluating basic function.</p>
<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_excerpts">
</div></div> 

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwMw" aria-labelledby="Smoke_testing"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Smoke_testing">Smoke testing</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Functional_testing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Smoke testing"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div class="excerpt-block" about="#mwt28" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwNA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Excerpt&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Excerpt&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Smoke testing (software)&quot;},&quot;only&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;paragraphs&quot;},&quot;paragraphs&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353838603" about="#mwt29" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Excerpt/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt30" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable dablink excerpt-hat selfref">These paragraphs are an excerpt from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke_testing_(software)" title="Smoke testing (software)">Smoke testing (software)</a>.<span class="mw-editsection-like plainlinks"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Smoke_testing_(software)&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Smoke_testing_(software)&amp;action=edit">edit</a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><div class="excerpt">
<p>In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_programming" title="Computer programming">computer programming</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_testing" title="Software testing">software testing</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke_testing_(software)" title="Smoke testing (software)">smoke testing</a> (also confidence testing, sanity testing,<sup about="#mwt31" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Smoke_testing_(software)_ISTQB_glossary_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Smoke testing (software) ISTQB glossary&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_ISTQB_glossary-6&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_ISTQB_glossary-6" id="mwNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup> build verification test (BVT)<sup about="#mwt33" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Smoke_testing_(software)_DustinRashkaPaul1999_7-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Smoke testing (software) DustinRashkaPaul1999&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_DustinRashkaPaul1999-7" id="mwOQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOw">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt37" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Smoke_testing_(software)_KanerBachPettichord2002_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Smoke testing (software) KanerBachPettichord2002&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_KanerBachPettichord2002-8&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_KanerBachPettichord2002-8" id="mwPQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPw">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt42" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-9&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-9" id="mwQQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQw">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRA">]</span></span></a></sup> and build acceptance test) is preliminary testing or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanity_testing" title="Sanity testing" class="mw-redirect">sanity testing</a> to reveal simple failures severe enough to, for example, reject a prospective software release. Smoke tests are a subset of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Test_case_(software)" title="Test case (software)">test cases</a> that cover the most important functionality of a component or system, used to aid assessment of whether main functions of the software appear to work correctly.<sup about="#mwt45" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Smoke_testing_(software)_ISTQB_glossary_6-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Smoke testing (software) ISTQB glossary&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_ISTQB_glossary-6" id="mwRQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwRg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRw">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt49" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Smoke_testing_(software)_DustinRashkaPaul1999_7-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Smoke testing (software) DustinRashkaPaul1999&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_DustinRashkaPaul1999-7&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_DustinRashkaPaul1999-7" id="mwSQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSw">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTA">]</span></span></a></sup> When used to determine if a computer program should be subjected to further, more fine-grained testing, a smoke test may be called a pretest<sup about="#mwt52" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-10&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-10" id="mwTQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTw">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUA">]</span></span></a></sup> or an intake test.<sup about="#mwt54" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Smoke_testing_(software)_ISTQB_glossary_6-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Smoke testing (software) ISTQB glossary&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_ISTQB_glossary-6" id="mwUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUw">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVA">]</span></span></a></sup> Alternatively, it is a set of tests run on each new build of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Product_(business)" title="Product (business)">product</a> to verify that the build is testable before the build is released into the hands of the test team.<sup about="#mwt58" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Smoke_testing_(software)_MenakerGuttigoli2014_11-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Smoke testing (software) MenakerGuttigoli2014&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_MenakerGuttigoli2014-11&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Smoke_testing_(software)_MenakerGuttigoli2014-11" id="mwVQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWA">]</span></span></a></sup> In the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DevOps" title="DevOps">DevOps</a> paradigm, use of a build verification test step is one hallmark of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Continuous_integration" title="Continuous integration">continuous integration</a> maturity stage.<sup about="#mwt61" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-12&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-12" id="mwWQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWw">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_excerpts">
</div></div> 

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwXQ" aria-labelledby="Regression_testing"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Regression_testing">Regression testing</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Functional_testing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Regression testing"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div class="excerpt-block" about="#mwt63" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwXg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Excerpt&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Excerpt&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Regression testing&quot;},&quot;only&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;paragraphs&quot;},&quot;paragraphs&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353838603" about="#mwt64" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Excerpt/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt65" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable dablink excerpt-hat selfref">These paragraphs are an excerpt from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regression_testing" title="Regression testing">Regression testing</a>.<span class="mw-editsection-like plainlinks"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Regression_testing&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Regression_testing&amp;action=edit">edit</a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><div class="excerpt">
<p><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regression_testing" title="Regression testing">Regression testing</a> (rarely, <i>non-regression testing</i><sup about="#mwt68" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-13&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-13" id="mwXw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwYA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYQ">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYg">]</span></span></a></sup>) is re-running functional and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-functional_testing" title="Non-functional testing">non-functional tests</a> to ensure that previously developed and tested software still performs as expected after a change.<sup about="#mwt73" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-14&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-14" id="mwYw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZQ">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZg">]</span></span></a></sup> If not, that would be called a <i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_regression" title="Software regression">regression</a></i>.</p>
<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_excerpts">
</div></div> 

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwZw" aria-labelledby="Usability_testing"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Usability_testing">Usability testing</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Functional_testing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Usability testing"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div class="excerpt-block" about="#mwt76" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwaA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Excerpt&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Excerpt&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Usability testing&quot;},&quot;only&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;paragraphs&quot;},&quot;paragraphs&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;1&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353838603" about="#mwt77" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Excerpt/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt78" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable dablink excerpt-hat selfref">These paragraphs are an excerpt from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usability_testing" title="Usability testing">Usability testing</a>.<span class="mw-editsection-like plainlinks"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Usability_testing&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Usability_testing&amp;action=edit">edit</a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><div class="excerpt">
<p><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usability_testing" title="Usability testing">Usability testing</a> is a technique used in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User-centered_design" title="User-centered design">user-centered</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interaction_design" title="Interaction design">interaction design</a> to evaluate a product by testing it on users. This can be seen as an irreplaceable <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usability" title="Usability">usability</a> practice, since it gives direct input on how real users use the system.<sup about="#mwt79" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-15&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-15" id="mwaQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaw">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbA">]</span></span></a></sup> It is more concerned with the design intuitiveness of the product and tested with users who have no prior exposure to it. Such testing is paramount to the success of an end product as a fully functioning application that creates confusion amongst its users will not last for long.<sup about="#mwt83" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-16&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-16" id="mwbQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbw">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcA">]</span></span></a></sup> This is in contrast with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usability_inspection" title="Usability inspection">usability inspection</a> methods where experts use different methods to evaluate a user interface without involving users.</p>
<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_excerpts">
</div></div>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwcQ" aria-labelledby="Six_steps"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Six_steps">Six steps</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Functional_testing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Six steps"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwcg">Functional testing typically involves six steps<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" about="#mwt86" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwcw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Citation needed&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Citation_needed&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;date&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;December 2010&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_December_2010" about="#mwt86"><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt86" id="mwdA"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (December 2010)">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup></p>

<ol id="mwdQ"><li id="mwdg">The identification of functions that the software is expected to perform</li>
<li id="mwdw">The creation of input data based on the function's specifications</li>
<li id="mweA">The determination of output based on the function's specifications</li>
<li id="mweQ">The execution of the test case</li>
<li id="mweg">The comparison of actual and expected outputs</li>
<li id="mwew">To check whether the application works as per the customer need</li></ol>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwfA" aria-labelledby="Open-source_tools"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Open-source_tools">Open-source tools</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Functional_testing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Open-source tools"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<p id="mwfQ">Several open-source tools support functional testing across web, mobile, and API applications. These include:</p>

<ul id="mwfg"><li id="mwfw">Selenium – Web browser automation</li>
<li id="mwgA">Playwright – Cross-browser end-to-end testing</li>
<li id="mwgQ">Robot Framework – Keyword-driven automation</li>
<li id="mwgg">Appium – Mobile application testing</li>
<li id="mwgw">SoapUI – API functional testing</li>
<li id="mwhA">Keploy – API testing and test generation</li></ul>

